Appendix F: Governance Window Margin

F.1 Definitions

Definition F.1 (Hazard Deadline). $T_H = H(z, E)$ is the minimum time until an irreversible hazardous consequence occurs, where $z \in \mathcal{Z}$ and $E$ is the environment state.

Definition F.2 (Detection Latency). $T_D = D(G, E)$ is the detection latency.

Definition F.3 (Intervention Latency). $T_I = I(G, E)$ is the intervention latency.

Definition F.4 (Governance Window Margin).

\mathrm{GWM} = T_H - T_D - T_I = H(z, E) - D(G, E) - I(G, E).

F.2 Dynamics

Theorem F.1 (GWM Dynamics). Under Assumption 2.3, if $H, D, I$ are continuously differentiable and $z(t), G(t), E(t)$ are differentiable in $t$, then

\frac{d}{dt} \mathrm{GWM} = H_z \dot{z} + H_E \dot{E} - D_G \dot{G} - D_E \dot{E} - I_G \dot{G} - I_E \dot{E}.

Equivalently,

\dot{\mathrm{GWM}} = H_z \dot{z} - (D_G + I_G) \dot{G} + (H_E - D_E - I_E) \dot{E}.

Proof. Apply the chain rule to each term:

\frac{d}{dt} H(z(t), E(t)) = H_z \dot{z} + H_E \dot{E},


\frac{d}{dt} D(G(t), E(t)) = D_G \dot{G} + D_E \dot{E},


\frac{d}{dt} I(G(t), E(t)) = I_G \dot{G} + I_E \dot{E}.

Subtracting gives the result. $\square$

Corollary F.1.1 (Sufficient Condition for Non-Decreasing GWM). A sufficient condition for $\dot{\mathrm{GWM}} \geq 0$ is

H_z \dot{z} + (H_E - D_E - I_E) \dot{E} \geq (D_G + I_G) \dot{G}.

Proof. From Theorem F.1, set $\dot{\mathrm{GWM}} \geq 0$ and isolate the governance adaptation term:

H_z \dot{z} + (H_E - D_E - I_E) \dot{E} - (D_G + I_G) \dot{G} \geq 0.

Rearranging gives the stated inequality. $\square$

Remark F.1. When $G$ is vector-valued, $D_G \dot{G}$ denotes the directional derivative $\langle \nabla_G D, \dot{G} \rangle$ and similarly for $I_G \dot{G}$.

