Appendix L: Open Problems

L.1 Computational Viability Theory

Exact computation of the viability kernel $\mathrm{Viab}_{F_G}(\mathcal{S})$ is intractable for general Marchaud dynamics. Approximation schemes with provable convergence rates remain an open research direction.

L.2 Tightness of Sensitivity Conditions

The weighted subgradient sensitivity condition is necessary but not sufficient for governability maintenance. Characterizing the gap between necessity and sufficiency remains open.

L.3 Optimal Pacing–Adaptation Mix

The control problem of choosing $(\dot{z}, \dot{G})$ to maintain $\mathcal{Q} \geq 0$ while minimizing cost is a constrained optimal control problem whose solution is not characterized in general.

L.4 Institutional Legitimacy

The problem of who has the authority to define, delegate, and revoke authority is outside the cryptographic boundary. A formal theory of legitimacy remains open.

L.5 Multi-Agent Governability

The extension of the GCP to multiple interacting governed agents with shared governance infrastructure remains open.

L.6 Robust vs Adaptive Trade-offs

Characterizing the conditions under which robust viability is achievable and quantifying the cost of robustness relative to adaptive viability is an open problem.

