Appendix M: Conclusion of the Appendices

The appendices provide the complete mathematical foundations for the Governance Control Plane. The central mathematical object is the viability kernel

\mathrm{Viab}_{F_G}(\mathcal{S}) = \{X \in \mathcal{S} : \exists \pi \ \forall t \geq 0, \ X_t^\pi \in \mathcal{S}\}.

Governability is the existence of an admissible governance policy capable of maintaining the evolving system inside the governable set. The four-way separation

\text{Intelligence} \neq \text{Capability} \neq \text{Authority} \neq \text{Governance}

constitutes the conceptual foundation of a formal architecture for governable autonomous intelligence.



